% refs.bib — bibliographic sources for ICCIT2026.tex
% POLICY (supervisor requirement): peer-reviewed publications only. No arXiv
% preprints, no workshop papers, no non-peer-reviewed technical reports.
% Every entry below corresponds to one of the 20 PDFs in the sibling
% `related papers` folder, and every entry is free to download:
%   * ACL Anthology      -> https://aclanthology.org/<anthology-id>/
%   * PMLR (ICML/CoRL)   -> https://proceedings.mlr.press/
%   * MLSys              -> https://proceedings.mlsys.org/
%   * AAAI OJS           -> https://ojs.aaai.org/
%   * IEEE Access        -> open access
%   * MIT Press CL       -> https://aclanthology.org/J08-4004.pdf (author copy)
% Venue coverage: IEEE Access, ACL, NAACL, EMNLP, EACL, LREC-COLING, COLING,
% IJCNLP-APACL, AAAI, ICML, MLSys, CoRL, SOSP, Computational Linguistics.
% The Llama-3.2/Gemma-3/Qwen3 checkpoints are distributed as version-tagged
% model releases and therefore have no bibliographic entry; provenance is
% given in Section III-B by exact runtime tag instead.
% SPACE: entries with 4+ authors are truncated to three plus `others`, which
% IEEEtran renders as `et al.` This keeps the reference list inside the
% six-page budget. Entries with <=3 authors list all authors.
% NOTE: local file paths are kept as plain %-comments (not a bib `note` field)
% because IEEEtran typesets `note` inline, and the long underscore-heavy
% filenames have no break points -- in the two-column IEEE layout they
% overrun the column width instead of wrapping. Comments never print.

